For the force cancellation (7.60), the first component gives $\alpha=\mathcal N(\alpha')$, where $\alpha'$ is defined by (7.30). We show that $\alpha'$ already lies in $\mathcal K$. Conditions (7.32)–(7.37) give $$\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
